# Development rules

- Specify the intended boundary and acceptance before implementation; link the owning ticket.
- Preserve Trigger fields/order across Solidity, shared types, and `docs/INTERFACE.md`.
- JPYC uses 18 decimals. Keep private identity data off-chain.
- Keep observed data, historical snapshots, forecasts, and synthetic scenarios distinct.
- Use Astro for the planned frontend. Map existing Next.js code as current code.
- Review affected source/spec areas before acknowledging their hashes; CI never acknowledges them.
- Generated graphs are local artifacts. Commit authored specs and review hashes only.
